<title>GERMANY: Fielmann has no comment on British group.</title>
<headline>Fielmann has no comment on British group.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>German optical retailer group Fielmann AG on Monday declined comment on a report that it was interested in taking over British optical optical retailing group Dolland &amp; Atchinson.</p>
<p>Germany's Platow Brief newsletter said in its latest edition that Fielmann was interested in acquiring Dolland &amp; Atchinson, one of the largest in Britain, in a deal that would make Fielmann the largest optical retail group in the world.</p>
<p>&quot;We will not comment on this rumour,&quot; a Fielmann spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
